  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At the qi sea banquet, Wu Ma Yang presents a floating shell that Eastern Sea immortals recognize as a small music clam shell, a rank seven immortal material. Music clams are ordinary clams that contain sound path dao marks: at desolate beast level they become giant music clams, then shrink again as ancient desolate beasts into small music clams. The specimen he shows is dead and without vitality, merely a rank seven sound path immortal material.",
      "chapters": [
        1885
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "small-music-clam",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_eastern_sea",
        "res_small_music_clam"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In Dragon Whale Paradise, Shen Cong Sheng pays Fang Yuan with a palm-sized desolate beast conch that stores wave sound. That wave sound is a sound path rank seven immortal material, a specialty product of Shen clan that can produce sounds for years without stopping. Fang Yuan names it constant wave sound when he takes the deal.",
      "chapters": [
        1895
      ],
